{% comment %}
  First-credit nudge: push body and email headline.

  Cases:
    1. Credit left + a saved restaurant  -> name the restaurant
    2. Credit left + nothing saved       -> Connected Content call for three nearby picks
    3. Nothing saved + the call fails    -> generic copy, still sends
    4. No credit, or balance missing     -> abort the send

  The Connected Content call only runs in case 2, so most sends make no
  external request. The endpoint is a placeholder for a recommendations
  service; attribute names are illustrative and map to inKind's schema.
{% endcomment %}

{% if custom_attribute.${wallet_balance} == blank or custom_attribute.${wallet_balance} <= 0 %}
  {% abort_message("no unspent credit") %}
{% endif %}

{% if custom_attribute.${saved_restaurants} != blank %}
Your ${{custom_attribute.${wallet_balance}}} is waiting at {{custom_attribute.${saved_restaurants} | first}}. Dinner tonight?
{% else %}
  {% connected_content https://api.example.com/v1/recommendations/nearby?user_id={{${user_id}}}&limit=3 :save recs :cache_max_age 900 :retry %}
  {% if recs.__http_status_code__ != 200 or recs.restaurants == blank %}
Your ${{custom_attribute.${wallet_balance}}} is waiting. Find a spot near you tonight.
  {% else %}
Your ${{custom_attribute.${wallet_balance}}} is waiting. Try {{recs.restaurants | map: 'name' | join: ', '}}.
  {% endif %}
{% endif %}
